{"actor":{"id":"claude-sonnet-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"Based on the README roadmap (I skipped everything already marked shipped), here's what I'd rank highest:\n\n**Quick, concrete bugs worth fixing next (cheap, real impact):**\n1. **`cledger export | head` crashes with unhandled EPIPE** — reproduces on any ledger piped into `head` or a command that exits early (confirmed on a 23MB ledger). Fix is a standard EPIPE handler; explicitly called out as deferred only because it \"wants its own change,\" not because it's hard.\n2. **The `>/dev/null 2>&1` on Gemini/Qwen hooks is probably dead weight** — added under a wrong theory about shell detachment; the real bug (unit mismatch on `timeout`) is already fixed. Removing it is flagged as \"the first thing to try,\" just never re-tested.\n3. **`cledger log` hides human-driven records by the wrong axis** — it keys hiding on event *kind* (session_state/activity/etc.) instead of *actor*, so a slash command you typed gets buried with token-count telemetry. `activity` already carries a real actor, so this is mostly wiring.\n\n**Correctness gaps with real (if narrower) blast radius:**\n4. **Reads default to unscoped** — push became branch-scoped in 0.14.0, but `readEvents`/`cledger export` still return every branch's conversations by default. This directly matters for intent-recall, which reads the library, not the CLI.\n5. **opencode capture is positional over a mutable store** — `session revert`/part deletion shifts indices, so a reverted session can duplicate events under new ids. Only bites opencode users who revert, but it's a live correctness bug, not theoretical.\n6. **Codex sub-agent coverage is unconfirmed** — Claude Code and opencode subagent capture are both verified; whether Codex writes a separate rollout for a sub-agent at all hasn't been checked. Worth a quick confirm since subagent capture is otherwise a shipped headline feature.\n\n**Bigger deferred features (larger scope, no shipped path yet):**\n7. **Post-push purge** — currently the *only* remedy for an already-shared secret is \"rotate the credential,\" since `cledger redact` refuses to touch pushed events. Three known hard parts (union-merge resurrection, host-side object retention window, preserving the redaction audit trail).\n8. **Forge PR/MR adapter** — review comments aren't captured at all yet; the `src/forge/` abstraction built for re-anchor suggestions already gives this a head start.\n9. New adapter backlog, if you want breadth over depth — Kimi CLI is next in line (append-only wire log, per-agent directories, Claude-Code-style hooks — closest fit to what cledger already knows how to ingest).\n\nMy pick if you want one thing to start today: **#1 (EPIPE)** — it's a real crash with a known fix and zero design decisions left to make. Want me to knock that out?","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"e9c918ccbe056afa89c6cdfa2dfe7c312545e44e","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:224d1239-00ba-4ddb-8117-5a487d569b0d","seq":47},"id":"ev1-ae2ce0f8009172cc13021ba79f1609b820d46cbe43c797af0a37f3cc542bb905","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-16T11:09:10.875Z","producer":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","session_id":"224d1239-00ba-4ddb-8117-5a487d569b0d","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.233","tool":"cledger","version":"0.21.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"text":"Based on the README roadmap (I skipped everything already marked shipped), here's what I'd rank highest:\n\n**Quick, concrete bugs worth fixing next (cheap, real impact):**\n1. **`cledger export | head` crashes with unhandled EPIPE** — reproduces on any ledger piped into `head` or a command that exits early (confirmed on a